            <ArticleTitle>Idiopathic isolated global T wave inversion: a report of 10 patients.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>944-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Ten patients (9 females and 1 male) between the age of 40-60 years with atypical chest pain and isolated global T wave inversion (in the absence of QRS complex or ST segment abnormality) and normal coronary arteries are described. The cause of these changes remains unknown.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
